{"url": "https://www.tue.nl/en/education/become-a-tue-student/tuition-fees-and-other-study-costs/application-fee", "final_url": "https://www.tue.nl/en/education/become-a-tue-student/tuition-fees-and-other-study-costs/application-fee", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Application fee\nSkip to content\nMenu\nClose the menu\nMenu\nEindhoven\nUniversity of\nTechnology\nEducation\nResearch\nOur university\nWorking at TU/e\nNews and Events\nImpact\nSearch\nNederlands\nNL\nSearch\nEducation\nWhy study at TU/e\nChallenge-Based Learning\nInternationally renowned research and education\nA great boost for your career\nExcellent atmosphere\nMore than a degree: where study meets career\nBachelor College\nBachelor's programs\nProgram structure\nSelection\nStudy-choice check\nHonors Academy\nTypes of universities\nUpcoming events\nPre-TU/e offer\nGraduate School\nMaster's programs\nHow we teach\nHonors Academy\nPre-Master\nEngD at TU/e\nPhD\nGraduate programs\nUpcoming events\nBecome a TU/e student\nAdmission and enrollment\nVisa & Residence Permit\nTuition fees and other study costs\nScholarships and grants\nHousing\nAcademy for Learning and Teaching\nAbout ALT\nTeacher Development\nLearning and Teaching Resources\nEducational Innovation and Development\nPartners\nEvents and News\nLearning Communities\nTU/e innovation Space\nAbout\nStudent\nTU/e staff\nPartners\nEducation Innovation projects\nTU/e Contest\nNews and Events\nProfessional Education\nHome\nEducation\nBecome a TU/e studen...\nTuition fees and oth...\nApplication fee\nFor international students\nApplication fee\nMenu\nTuition fees and other study costs\nApplication fee\nTuition fee\nPayment options\nRefunding tuition fees\nRequest a Proof of Paid Tuition Fees (BBC)\nGuarantee fee\nHow to pay the guarantee fee\nProof of financial means\nNote: The information on this page applies to applications for the academic year 2027\u20132028.\nApplicants who have completed their previous education outside the Netherlands or at an international school within the Netherlands are required to pay a non-refundable application fee of \u20ac100 per application.\nThis fee covers the additional administrative costs incurred during the admissions process that are associated with evaluating academic transcripts and any supporting documents that need to be verified manually.\nProof of payment must be uploaded in the online application form. A copy of your bank transfer order is sufficient.\nPlease note: if the full fee is not received, we will unfortunately be unable to process your application.\nThe application fee cannot be paid in cash, by credit card, by banker's draft, or by cheque. It is also not to pay in installments.\nPayment instructions\nTo transfer the application fee from a foreign bank account, please use the following details on on your international bank transfer form:\nBank account number TU/e: 1148.70.438\nName of bank: Rabobank\nBeneficiary: Technische Universiteit Eindhoven (please use this Dutch version of the TU/e name as this is registered at the bank)\nIBAN-code: NL66 RABO 0114 8704 38\nBIC-code: RABONL2U (if you need a BIC-code with 11 digits, you can enter: RABONL2UXXX))\nCity: Eindhoven, the Netherlands\nAddress: Postbus 301 \u2013 5600 AH Eindhoven, The Netherlands\nReference:\nYour full name and date of birth (especially important if someone else is making the payment)\nYour student number\nAmount: \u20ac 100\nEnsure that the full amount is received by TU/e. Any bank transfer fees must be paid in addition to the application fee. TU/e must not be charged for these costs.\nExemption for countries where restrictive measures (sanctions) are in force\nDue to international sanctions, TU/e is unable to accept direct or indirect financial transactions from or involving the following countries: Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Russia, Sudan, and Syria.\nIf you reside in or hold the nationality of one of these countries\u202f and do not have a SEPA (IBAN) bank account, do not transfer the application fee. Instead, please provide the requested details in the OSIRIS application form.\nHave a question?\nFill in the contact form below and our team will get back to you.\nName\n*\nEmail\n*\nMessage\n*\nSend message\nBachelor programs\nMaster programs\nAdmission and enrollment\nWorking at TU/e\nSearch staff\nRoute & map\nEducation Guide\nIntranet\nCursor\nNavigation address\nDe Zaale\nEindhoven\nPhone number:\n+31 (0)40 247 9111\nContact\nPostal address\nPO Box 513\n5600 MB Eindhoven\nFollow us\nLike TU/e on Facebook\nFollow TU/e on LinkedIn\nFollow TU/e on YouTube\n\u00a9 2026 TU/e\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy\nEindhoven\nUniversity of\nTechnology\nEducation\nResearch\nOur university\nWorking at TU/e\nNews and Events\nImpact\nTU/e Image Bank\nEducationguide\nIntranet\nCursor\nEducation\nEducation\nEducation\nWhy study at TU/e\nBachelor College\nGraduate School\nBecome a TU/e student\nAcademy for Learning and Teaching\nTU/e innovation Space\nProfessional Education\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nInstitutes\nResearch Areas\nResearch Groups\nResearch Labs\nResearch Projects\nResearchers\nDepartments\nGrants & Awards\nResearch Support\nOur university\nOur university\nOur university\nAbout the University\nDepartments\nCalendar and events\nTU/e Campus\nLibrary\nCommunity\nStudent Teams\nWorking at TU/e\nWorking at TU/e\nWorking at TU/e\nVacancies\nScientific Staff\nSupport Staff\nPhD\nEngD\nAt TU/e\nNews and Events\nNews and Events\nNews and Events\nNews overview\nMedia relations\nImpact\nImpact\nImpact\nCooperation with Industry\nKnowledge Transfer Office\nTU/e Participations\nStarting your business\nIntellectual Property\nStay rates\nBrainport for Eachother\nTU/e Image Bank\nEducationguide\nIntranet\nCursor", "links": [["Skip to content", "https://www.tue.nl/en/education/become-a-tue-student/tuition-fees-and-other-study-costs/application-fee#mainContent"], ["Eindhoven University of Technology", "https://www.tue.nl/en/"], ["Education", "ht